# type-fest before a new type

`type-fest` is a dependency. Before declaring a type that transforms, narrows, brands, or reshapes another type, search the installed package for that name.

`node_modules` lives in the container volume, so search there:

```bash
docker exec -u 1000:1000 boilerplate-next-dev grep -n "Except" node_modules/type-fest/index.d.ts node_modules/type-fest/readme.md
```

Replace `Except` with the type you were about to write. The index exports it as `export type {Except}`. Also check "Alternative type names" in the readme (`Prettify` is `Simplify`, `MaybePromise` is `Promisable`).

If it exists, import it. Do not copy the definition.

```ts
import type { Except } from "type-fest"

type FooWithoutRainbow = Except<Foo, "rainbow">
```

A product type (`User`, `Invoice`) stays in the app. Built-in utilities (`Partial`, `Pick`, `Omit`, `Awaited`, `Record`) stay built-in. Names type-fest declined (`Dictionary`, `Nullish`, `Diff`) stay declined; use the alternative documented under "Declined types".
